speechtext:
Extract from the minutes of a meeting of the board of directors of the Canadian Pacific Railway Company, duly called and held at the principal office of the company, at Montreal, on Monday, August 10, 1908.
Whereas the authorized ordinary capital stock of this company at this date is $150,000,000 divided into 1,500,000 shares of the par or face value of $100 each;
And whereas pursuant to the provisions of section 3 of the Act 55-56, Victoria, chapter 35, Canada, the company being duly authorized in that behalf by its shareholders at a special general meeting duly called for the purpose, may from time to time increase its capital stock for any purpose for which the company requires new capital, to such amounts and at such times as the shareholders at any such meeting may determine, such issue being first approved by the Governor in Council;
And whereas the company requires from time to time new capital for the purposes of its undertaking, and it is desirable to increase the amount of the said authorized ordinary capital stock to $200,000,000, being an increase of $50,000,000:
Now therefore it is resolved as follows, that is to say:-
That it is in the interests of this comnany that the ordinary capital stock of the company be increased from $150,000,000 to an amount not exceeding $200,000,000 in shares of $100 each or its equivalent in sterling money of Great Britain, to be issued and sold for the purposes of its undertaking as may be determined by resolution of the shareholders of the company ;
2.	That the president of the company be, and he is hereby authorized to make an application in the name of the comnany to the Governor in Council to have the said proposed increase of stock duly approved of;
3.	That the secretary of Ahe company be and he is hereby authorized and directed to give notice in the manner and form provided by the statutes and by-laws relating thereto for the holding of a special general meeting
